<!--
READ 1000 — Temperance  (Activity bank)

A lo-blocks build of "Design_docs/Temperance/Temperance_Module_072826.pdf",
with one deliberate departure from that document:
  * "Joe's notes" (the note-checking matrix) tests the TEXTBOOK excerpt, not
    the lecture.

Layout (see temperance_module_full_sba_part1.olx). The tab strip is the top
level; its first tab, "Main Content," is the session itself:
  * Left  pane : the scripted small-group conversation
                 (temperance_module_full_dialogue_part1.chatpeg). Peers Danielle,
                 Joe, and Karis and the reading instructor Professor Booker.
  * Right pane : a UseHistory (temperance_pane) the conversation drives with
                 target embeds — `::screen [display=target:temperance_pane ...]`,
                 explained in the chatpeg's header comment.
Each READING screen below — the lecture, the four textbook parts, the
lithograph — also gets its own tab, via <Use ref="..."> of the same block, so a
student can reopen it (with their own highlights) at any point.

The textbook is CHUNKED across four Main Content readings (temperance_read_1/a2/b/c),
one per paragraph, so peer dialogue can mediate each passage before the next
appears and before the items that depend on it.
This FULL build carries the module through all five parts: textbook, lithograph,
article, a then/now synthesis, and Pulling It Together — the culminating
four-or-five-sentence synthesis.
     -->

