<Vertical id="temperance_notes">
<Markdown id="temperance_notes_prompt">
## Checking Joe's Notes on the Textbook

Joe made a list of what he thought were the important points from the *American
Yawp* excerpt. For **each statement**, decide whether it is **correct and central
to the text**, **correct but less important**, or **not correct**. Then press
**Submit**.
</Markdown>
<CapaProblem id="temperance_notes_problem" title="Joe's Notes on the Textbook" maxAttempts="1" showAnswer="attempted" answerReveal="auto" lockInput="closed">
<TabularMCQGrader id="temperance_notes_grader">
<TabularMCQ id="temperance_notes_grid">
cols:
  - Correct and central to the text
  - Correct but less important
  - Not correct
rows:
  - "The Second Great Awakening revitalized Christian faith and inspired both personal and social reform.|n_awakening[Correct and central to the text]"
  - "Lyman Beecher championed the temperance movement.|n_beecher[Correct but less important]"
  - "Middle-class women played a leading role in reform activity.|n_women[Correct and central to the text]"
  - "The Industrial Revolution was a response to increasing social problems and urban growth.|n_indrev[Not correct]"
  - "The Benevolent Empire was a powerful network that melded religion and reform.|n_network[Correct and central to the text]"
  - "Social reform societies grew significantly between 1815 and 1861.|n_societies[Correct but less important]"
</TabularMCQ>
</TabularMCQGrader>
</CapaProblem> <!-- temperance_notes_problem -->
</Vertical> <!-- temperance_notes -->


